// reviews pack -- projections (epic memql#5532, issue memql#5553).
//
// A CONCEPT FIELD IS NOT A READABLE FIELD. A query with no shape answers the
// graph bundle, whose payload fields sit one level down -- so a caller
// reading `row.body` off it gets "" and no error, which is the failure mode
// this file exists to remove. Every read in this pack names a shape.
//
// TWO PROJECTIONS OF ONE CONCEPT, and the difference between them is a
// security property rather than tidiness: reviewPublic omits authorEmail,
// so the shopper's address never reaches the read whose output is served to
// an unauthenticated browser. The Go half also declines to project it, and
// that belt-and-braces is deliberate -- the DSL half is what makes the
// omission survive somebody later writing a second caller.

use reviews.concepts.{ review, moderationAction, reviewSettings }

@description("A review as its MERCHANT sees it, including the shopper's email so they can reply. Never served to a storefront.")
@row
shape review reviewFull {
  row.id
  ownerUserId
  storeId
  siteId
  productHandle
  productId
  title
  body
  rating
  authorName
  authorEmail
  imageAttachmentIds
  createdAtClient
  row.createdAt
}

@description("A review as a STOREFRONT may render it. authorEmail is absent, and its absence is the point: it exists so a merchant can reply, not so the internet can harvest it, and this is the projection behind the one read an unauthenticated browser reaches.")
@row
shape review reviewPublic {
  row.id
  storeId
  productHandle
  title
  body
  rating
  authorName
  createdAtClient
  row.createdAt
}

@description("A moderation decision, whole. Append-only, so a row is a decision and this is all of it.")
@row
shape moderationAction moderationActionFull {
  row.id
  reviewId
  storeId
  criterion
  decidedBy
  principalKind
  note
  row.createdAt
}

@description("One store's reviews settings.")
@row
shape reviewSettings reviewSettingsFull {
  row.id
  ownerUserId
  storeId
  publicDisplay
  criteriaText
  row.createdAt
}
